Make shuf choose each swap partner uniformly. It took rand() modulo the
number of lines left, XORing in a second rand() shifted by 15 bits only
when that number exceeded RAND_MAX. Where RAND_MAX is 32767, as on
Windows, the value had 15 bits for up to 32767 lines, so the remainder
was strongly biased: from 20000 lines, "shuf -n 1" picked each of the
first 12768 twice as often as each of the others. With more lines it
had 30 bits and could never pick a line past 2^30. Where RAND_MAX is
2^31-1, the remainder was likewise biased once the number of lines was
a large fraction of 2^31, and beyond that the shift overflowed int.

Build 32 random bits from three rand() calls, 15 bits each, and reject
values below 2^32 % n so that every remainder in [0, n) is equally
likely.

---
 coreutils/shuf.c |   29 +++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

--- a/coreutils/shuf.c
+++ b/coreutils/shuf.c
@@ -37,6 +37,24 @@
 #define OPT_z		(1 << 4)
 #define OPT_STR		"ei:n:o:z"
 
+/* Return a uniformly distributed random number in [0, n) */
+static uint32_t random_below(uint32_t n)
+{
+	uint32_t r;
+	uint32_t min = -n % n; /* 2^32 % n */
+
+	/* RAND_MAX can be as small as 32767: make 32 random bits from
+	 * three calls, and reject the values below 2^32 % n so that
+	 * every remainder is equally likely.
+	 */
+	do {
+		r = rand() & 0x7fff;
+		r = (r << 15) | (rand() & 0x7fff);
+		r = (r << 15) | (rand() & 0x7fff);
+	} while (r < min);
+	return r % n;
+}
+
 /*
  * Use the Fisher-Yates shuffle algorithm on an array of lines.
  * If the required number of output lines is less than the total
@@ -48,16 +66,7 @@
 
 	while (outlines != 0) {
 		char *tmp;
-		unsigned r = rand();
-		/* RAND_MAX can be as small as 32767 */
-		if (numlines > RAND_MAX)
-			r ^= rand() << 15;
-		r %= numlines;
-//TODO: the above method is seriously non-uniform when numlines is very large.
-//For example, with numlines of   0xf0000000,
-//values of (r % numlines) in [0, 0x0fffffff] range
-//are more likely: e.g. r=1 and r=0xf0000001 both map to 1,
-//whereas only one value, r=0xefffffff, maps to 0xefffffff.
+		unsigned r = random_below(numlines);
 		numlines--;
 		tmp = lines[numlines];
 		lines[numlines] = lines[r];
